{"name":"Easy on the Eyes","hex":"#f9ecb6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"easy on the eyes","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Physically attractive; beautiful."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/easy_on_the_eyes"}],"entries":[{"title":"Easy on the Eyes","blocks":[{"text":"\"Easy on the Eyes\" is a 1952 single by Eddy Arnold, written by Arnold and songwriter Cy Coben. \"Easy on the Eyes\" was Eddy Arnold's forty-sixth entry on the Country & Western chart. The single went to number one on the Best Seller list with a total of fourteen weeks on the chart."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Easy_on_the_Eyes","wikidata":"Q5331185"},{"title":"Eye","blocks":[{"text":"An eye is a sensory organ that allows an organism to perceive visual information. It detects light and converts it into electro-chemical impulses in neurons (neurones). It is part of an organism's visual system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Krilleyekils.jpg/330px-Krilleyekils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye","wikidata":"Q7364"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Bison_bonasus_right_eye_close-up.jpg/500px-Bison_bonasus_right_eye_close-up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Bison_bonasus_right_eye_close-up.jpg/500px-Bison_bonasus_right_eye_close-up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Eye of a European bison","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABison_bonasus_right_eye_close-up.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/%D0%93%D0%BE%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%BE%D0%B9_%D0%B3%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B7.jpg/500px-%D0%93%D0%BE%D0%BB%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%BE%D0%B9_%D0%B3%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%B7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_ca